{{Quote|There were dissidents on Anoat. No one could find it. So they gassed the planet.|Tam Bastion, to Riley's sibling|<ref name="Star Wars: Uprising">''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]''</ref>}}
Around [[0 ABY]]<ref name="Date" /> the [[planet]] of [[Anoat]] was '''gassed''' by the [[Galactic Empire]]. A group of [[Anoat dissidents|dissidents]] were known to have been present on Anoat, but the Empire could not find their [[Unidentified Anoat dissident base|camp]]. Consequently, [[Captain]] [[Ubrik Adelhard]],<ref name="SM: The Truth of Anoat" /> a junior military advisor<ref name="Star Wars: Uprising" /> in command of his own [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyer]],<ref name="Jakku">[[Battle of Jakku — Insurgency Rising 1|''Battle of Jakku — Insurgency Rising'' 1]]</ref> decided to gas the whole planet, rendering Anoat toxic and [[poison]]ous, and forcing much of the population to flee their [[homeworld]].<ref name="SM: The Truth of Anoat" /> Those who did not evacuate the planet ended up mutating, transforming into feral creatures known as [[Lurker (Anoat)|Lurkers]].<ref name="SM: Heading to Anoat" /> The gassing of Anoat also taught the Alliance a valuable lesson, which was to avoid operating among civilians.<ref name="SM: The Truth of Anoat" />

The Empire's official version was that Anoat had been poisoned and a few of its inhabitants "moderately damaged" by "a series of tragic industrial accidents."<ref name="MC: Anoat">''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]''&mdash;Mercenary Contract: "Anoat"</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The gassing of Anoat was first mentioned in the [[2015]] [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Star Wars: Uprising]]'', and dates the event several years before the Battle of Yavin.<ref name="SM: Heading to Anoat" /> The event was later first depicted in the [[2024]] comic [[Battle of Jakku — Insurgency Rising 1|''Battle of Jakku — Insurgency Rising'' 1]]. However, ''Insurgency Rising'' 1 conflicts with ''Uprising''{{'s}} dating of the event, as the comic shows Ubrik Adelhard being summoned by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] to the ''[[Executor]]'' immediately following the event.<ref name="Jakku" /> The ''Executor'' is completed shortly after the events of the comic [[Darth Vader (2015) 25|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 25]], which is set post-Yavin and is dated to [[0 ABY]] by the reference book ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''.<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> As a result, this article treats the date of pre-Yavin as an error.<ref name="Date" />

